// Lily# - Music notation compiler
// AUTO-GENERATED by audit/scripts/Extract-EmmentalerSkylines.py — DO NOT EDIT MANUALLY.
// Re-run the script after the bundled Emmentaler font is updated.
// Source font: LilySharp.Core/Fonts/emmentaler-20.otf
//
// Accidental horizontal skylines, taken from each glyph's REAL outline the way
// LilyPond builds them: lily/accidental.cc:48 horizontal_skylines ->
// skylines_from_stencil -> add_outline_to_skyline (lily/freetype.cc:175), cubics
// flattened to max(2, len/0.2) segments, classified by contour orientation
// (Emmentaler is CFF => CCW). The effective outline->stencil scale is 1.0 for
// accidentals, so a skyline coordinate is just the outline in staff spaces
// (1 ss = unitsPerEm/4 = 250 font units). These are RAW outlines: the flat
// 0.375 fattening (accidental.cc:65-82, skipped when parenthesized) and the
// courtesy paren composition (accidental.cc:33-43 parenthesize) are runtime
// branches in AccidentalPlacement.GlyphSkylinePair, where LilyPond has them.
//
//
// Clef VERTICAL skylines, from the same outline flattening on the other horizon
// axis: scm/define-grobs.scm:902-927 gives Clef grob::always-vertical-skylines-from-stencil.
//
// The outline->stencil ratio lily/stencil-integral.cc:551-557 divides by,
//     scale = bbox[X_AXIS].length () / real_bbox[X_AXIS].length ()
// is COMPUTED here rather than assumed (glyph_outline_scale): bbox is FreeType's
// glyph metrics under FT_LOAD_NO_SCALE (freetype.cc:51-65
// ly_FT_get_unscaled_indexed_char_dimensions), i.e. the CONTROL box, and real_bbox
// is the exact outline box (freetype.cc:67-88 uses FT_Outline_Get_BBox). It comes
// out at exactly 1.0 for every glyph baked here -- which is what LilyPond's own
// comment at :549-550 predicts -- but it is a division in LilyPond, so it is a
// division here, and the generator writes a NOTE to stderr if any glyph ever
// leaves 1.0. Writing 1 instead would be folding an evaluated result.
// A pair of BOXES makes two facing clefs bind at the sum of their maxima; a pair of
// OUTLINES binds lower, because the G clef's deepest ink is at x=1.84 and its highest
// at x=2.228. Measured off LilyPond in audit/lp-geometry/probes/skyline-binding.ly:
// dist(upper DOWN, lower UP) = 7.210039 against 3.540000 + 3.776000 = 7.316000.
//
// fetaText dynamic letter VERTICAL skylines + GPOS kerns, for DynamicText's own
// profile (my_dim): scm/define-grobs.scm:1446 declares vertical-skylines from the
// stencil, and side-position-interface.cc:353-358 measures the support distance
// POINTWISE against it — a \f tucks beside a thin stem sliver, a \fff binds on it
// (audit/lp-geometry/probes/dynamic-support.ly DSQ vs DMF). Letters compose at pen
// positions = hmtx advance (DynamicLetter*Advance, Extract-EmmentalerMetrics.py) +
// DynamicLetterKern below; the composition X model and every kern pair are measured
// in audit/lp-geometry/probes/dynamic-text-x.ly, whose header also names the
// per-glyph Pango shaping quantisation (<= 0.0167 ss, both signs) that stays a
// residual family rather than being fitted.
//
// Each array is a flat list of skyline BUILDINGS, four doubles apiece:
//   start (horizon low), startValue (sky*other at horizon low),
//   endValue (sky*other at horizon high), end (horizon high)
// — the sign-framed form SkylineBuilding takes. The horizon is Y for the accidental
// pairs (sky = -1 LEFT, +1 RIGHT) and X for the clefs (sky = -1 DOWN, +1 UP).
//
// ⚠️ A LIST IS NOT ONE SIDE OF THE GLYPH, AND MIXED SIGNS ARE NOT A BUG. Edges are
// sorted by CONTOUR DIRECTION, not by which half of the glyph they sit in
// (lily/include/lazy-skyline-pair.hh:53-65 add_contour_segment), so a glyph with
// counters or with two arms puts edges with POSITIVE y into its DOWN array and
// edges with NEGATIVE y into its UP array. ClefSkyCD really does carry buildings
// at y = +1.96, and LilyPond's own lists carry the same ones; the skyline RESOLVE
// picks the right building at each x. Dropping them by sign would delete real
// silhouette. Checked against LilyPond's ly:skyline->points dump for all three
// clefs (audit/lp-geometry/probes/skyline-binding.ly): six digits, every vertex.

